(Unprivileged, mknod(2) refuses a character device with EPERM, so the)
(statement sets the error flag and the program carries on. The packing)
(of 259:300 itself is pinned by the codegen unit tests.)
Delete the file "/tmp/vox_test_740_device".

Create a device node called "/tmp/vox_test_740_device" with type "c" major 259 minor 300.
On error print "refused, numbers written out".

a number called major is 259.
a number called minor is 300.
Create a device node called "/tmp/vox_test_740_device" with type "c" major major minor minor.
On error print "refused, numbers worked out at run time".

Print "carried on".
